Consider the following C function:

```c
int fun(int n) {
    if (n <= 1)
        return 1;
    if (n % 2 == 0)
        return fun(n / 2) + n;
    else
        return fun(n - 1) * 2;
}
```

What is the return value of `fun(7)`?

Consider the following C function that takes a pointer to the head of a non-empty singly linked list of integers:

```c
struct Node {
    int data;
    struct Node *next;
};

int fun(struct Node *head) {
    if (head == NULL) return 0;
    if (head->next == NULL) return head->data;
    return head->data - fun(head->next);
}
```

If the linked list contains the values `1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5` in that order (with `head` pointing to the node containing `1`), what is the value returned by `fun(head)`?

Consider the following C function definition:

```c
int foo(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) return 0;
    return n + foo(n - 2);
}
```

